<title>UK: New UK parliament to convene on May 7.</title>
<headline>New UK parliament to convene on May 7.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's House of Commons will reconvene on May 7 after an election on May 1, officials said.</p>
<p>Speaking after Conservative Prime Minister John Major named May 1 as the election date, the officials said members of parliament would be sworn and a new Speaker elected on May 7.</p>
<p>The state opening of parliament will take place a week later, on May 14, officials said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
